lesson: 217
title: Corners of bunting flags
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A triangle has 3 corners and 3 sides; a square and a rectangle each have 4 corners and 4 sides.
explain: When shapes of two kinds are mixed, count the corners of each kind on its own and then add.
explain: Bunting with 5 triangle flags and 4 square flags: 5 × 3 = 15 and 4 × 4 = 16, so 15 + 16 = 31 corners.
vars: a=name t=3..15 q=2..10 z=2..9
answer: t * 3 + q * 4
exercise: {a} cuts out {t} triangle flags and {q} square flags for the bunting. How many corners do the flags have?
exercise: A string of bunting has {t} triangular flags and {q} square ones. How many corners are there altogether?
exercise: The garden path has {t} triangle stones and {q} square stones. How many corners do the stones have in all?
exercise: {a} sticks {t} triangles and {q} rectangles on a poster. How many corners do the shapes have?
exercise: How many corners are there on {t} triangle tiles and {q} square tiles?
exercise: For the fair, {a} paints a gold dot on every corner of {t} triangle flags and {q} square flags. How many dots does {a.he} paint?
exercise: bunting: {t} triangles n {q} squares. how many corners
exercise: {a} made {t+1} triangle flags, no hang on, {t}, plus {q} square ones. corners?
exercise: {a} says a triangle has 4 corners lol. no. {t} triangle flags + {q} square flags, corners
exercise: cut out {t} triangles and {q} rectangles for art, {z} glue sticks gone already. how many corners
exercise: {q} squares n {t} triangles on the fridge. corners total?
test: Every corner of {q} square cards and {t} triangle cards gets a sticker. How many stickers are used?
test: What is the total number of corners of {t} triangles together with {q} rectangles?
test: {q} square tiles are laid next to {t} triangular tiles. Find the number of corners.
test: The bunting over the school gate has {q} square flags and {t} triangle flags, and {z} balloons hang beside it. How many corners do the flags have?
test: triangle flags {t}, square flags {q}. how many corners
test: decorating for nan's party, {t} triangles n {q} squares of bunting. how many corners need tape
exam: A length of bunting bears {t} triangular pennants and {q} square pennants. Determine the aggregate number of corners of the said pennants.
exam: Given that {t.words} triangles and {q.words} rectangles are affixed to a display board, ascertain the total number of vertices.
exam: Compute the number of corners to be reinforced, each corner of {q} square flags and {t} triangular flags requiring reinforcement.
exam: It is given that a pathway is laid with {t} triangular and {q} square paving stones. State the number of corners of the paving stones.
exercise: The street-party bunting had {t} triangle flags and {q+2} square flags, but the neighbour's dog "left a present" on 2 of the square ones and they were thrown away. How many corners do the flags that are left have?
exercise: council "restructured the budget" so we only got {t} triangle flags n {q} square ones, cheapskates. how many corners
test: {a} fudged the figures: {a.he} said {a.he} had cut out {t+q+5} flags, but there are only {t} triangles and {q} squares. How many corners do the flags that really exist have?
